/// Blood (Deoxygenated). The color of blood depends on its oxygen level. When
/// hemoglobin has a full oxygen load, it has a bright red color, and when it's
/// deoxygenated it's a darker red. For example, arterial and capillary blood
/// is bright, and venous blood is dark. Upon exposure to air, deoxygenated
/// blood quickly oxygenates and turns a brighter shade of red. Source: Blood.
/// Returns material and colour.
@material bloodDeoxygenated() {
  return [[0, 0, 1.35, 0], [0, 0, 0, 0], [1, 0.8, 0, 0], [0, 0, 0, 0]], [0.6763, 0, 0];
}
/// Density of blood (Deoxygenated), kg/m^3.
bloodDeoxygenatedDensity = 1060;

/// Blood (Oxygenated). The color of blood depends on its oxygen level. When
/// hemoglobin has a full oxygen load, it has a bright red color, and when it's
/// deoxygenated it's a darker red. For example, arterial and capillary blood
/// is bright, and venous blood is dark. Upon exposure to air, deoxygenated
/// blood quickly oxygenates and turns a brighter shade of red. Source: Blood.
/// Returns material and colour.
@material bloodOxygenated() {
