/// Water. While relatively small quantities of water appear to be colorless,
/// pure water has a slight blue color that becomes deeper as the thickness of
/// the observed sample increases beyond 50 cm. The hue of water is an
/// intrinsic property and is caused by selective absorption and scattering of
/// white light. Dissolved elements or suspended impurities may give water a
/// different color. Source: Refractive index database. Returns material and
/// colour.
@material water() {
  return [[0, 0, 1.3325, 0], [0, 0, 0, 0], [1, 1000, 0, 0], [0, 0, 0, 0]], [0.9862, 0.9982, 0.9987];
}
